  "description": "The \u0027dss_clusters_cached\u0027 dataset provides detailed information about various clusters, including their identifiers, types, and usage metrics. This dataset is particularly useful for managing and monitoring clusters within a data science platform. Each cluster is uniquely identified by an \u0027id\u0027 and has a \u0027name\u0027 for easy reference. The \u0027type\u0027 column indicates how the cluster was set up, such as manually, while the \u0027architecture\u0027 column describes the system design, like KUBERNETES. The \u0027state\u0027 column provides the current status of the cluster, which is crucial for operational monitoring. Additionally, the dataset includes usage metrics such as \u0027usedInScenarios\u0027 and \u0027usedInProjects\u0027, which show how many scenarios and projects utilize each cluster, respectively. This information can help in assessing the importance and workload of each cluster. The \u0027owner\u0027 column identifies the person responsible for the cluster, ensuring accountability and management. Finally, the \u0027url\u0027 column provides a direct link to the cluster\u0027s details, facilitating easy access and management. This dataset is essential for administrators and data scientists who need to keep track of cluster configurations and their utilization across different projects and scenarios.",
